The program of run-arrays.mt, run on the machine's GPU for float and for
float32: the arrays the region updates are mapped tofrom, over their
headers' and elements' words. A region whose procedure updates an array,
which its operations do not show, maps each array of the type tofrom and
finds which one it gives (design document, "What is lowered so far"), so
the array it only reads is copied back too, unchanged. float32's arrays
are packed 4 bytes to an element, so they map fewer bytes: 3 elements and
the header are 24 bytes, not 32, and 4 elements 24, not 40.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: %instantiate %S/run-arrays.mt float %t.float.d
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %t.float.d/run_arrays_float.m -o %t.float
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIBOMPTARGET_INFO=1 %t.float 2> %t.float.info \
RUN:   | FileCheck %S/run-arrays.mt --check-prefix=OUTPUT-FLOAT --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FLOAT < %t.float.info
FLOAT: info: Entering OpenMP kernel at {{.*}}run_arrays_float.m:{{[0-9]+}}:5 with 6 arguments:
FLOAT-NEXT: info: to(region_slot)[8]
FLOAT-NEXT: info: tofrom(A)[32]
FLOAT-NEXT: info: tofrom(STATE_VARIABLE_B_0)[40]
FLOAT: info: Entering OpenMP kernel at {{.*}}run_arrays_float.m:{{[0-9]+}}:5 with 7 arguments:
FLOAT-NEXT: info: to(region_slot)[8]
FLOAT-NEXT: info: tofrom(STATE_VARIABLE_B_0)[16]
FLOAT-NEXT: info: tofrom(STATE_VARIABLE_C_0)[24]
FLOAT-NOT: Entering OpenMP kernel

RUN: %instantiate %S/run-arrays.mt float32 %t.float32.d
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %t.float32.d/run_arrays_float32.m -o %t.float32
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIBOMPTARGET_INFO=1 %t.float32 2> %t.float32.info \
RUN:   | FileCheck %S/run-arrays.mt --check-prefix=OUTPUT-FLOAT32 --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FLOAT32 < %t.float32.info
FLOAT32: info: Entering OpenMP kernel at {{.*}}run_arrays_float32.m:{{[0-9]+}}:5 with 6 arguments:
FLOAT32-NEXT: info: to(region_slot)[8]
FLOAT32-NEXT: info: tofrom(A)[24]
FLOAT32-NEXT: info: tofrom(STATE_VARIABLE_B_0)[24]
FLOAT32: info: Entering OpenMP kernel at {{.*}}run_arrays_float32.m:{{[0-9]+}}:5 with 7 arguments:
FLOAT32-NEXT: info: to(region_slot)[8]
FLOAT32-NEXT: info: tofrom(STATE_VARIABLE_B_0)[16]
FLOAT32-NEXT: info: tofrom(STATE_VARIABLE_C_0)[24]
FLOAT32-NOT: Entering OpenMP kernel
